{"_provenance":"SYNTHESISED, and only in two named places. Base: tests/fixtures/muse-code/echo-session-1.1.1.jsonl, itself a real Muse Code 1.1.1 log. Two fields were ADDED to it because a --provider echo run cannot produce them and no paid Meta session was available: (1) `model_id` on runtime.session.metadata.record, inserted directly after `provider_id`; (2) `model` on the model_completed event. Both spellings and both positions are taken from the field-name literals of the binary's own serde structs recovered from ~/.local/bin/muse-bin-1.1.1-R2514.1: `SessionMetadata` lays out provider_id/model_id/web_search_mode/tool_surface_version, and the model_completed event lays out usage/duration_ms/finish_reason/model. The token counts were also raised off zero so the pricing path is exercised; the echo run's real counters are all 0. provider_id was changed from \"echo\" to \"meta\". Everything else is the real log, unmodified. A real --provider meta session must replace this file."}
